      "answer": "The approved live patch window for Verdant Bay is on 2026-03-24 from 02:00 to 04:00 local time. If validation checks fail during the live patch, the rollback procedure is to run the command `orchestrator rollback --target ruleset=<prior_sha>`, which rehydrates the prior ruleset and replays the invalidation hook. After rollback, the steps include notifying Verdant Bay, opening an incident for manual remediation, and reverting any partial replays. The validation checks involve running 50 synthetic approval flows plus a sample of 50 in-flight approvals marked by the customer, and if any validation fails, the rollback is triggered automatically [art_fff67d92fe41]. \n\nExact detailed step-by-step instructions beyond the command usage and post-rollback steps are not provided in the evidence, nor are the specific validation criteria fully enumerated beyond \"if any validation fails\" [art_fff67d92fe41].",
