      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Merchant Services used \"businessUnit=merchant\" while Payments Ops used \"department=payments.\" This inconsistency caused the ingestion normalization to fail collapsing these into a single canonical attribute, leading to Rules Engine matching failures on the entity tag used for routing approvals.\n\nJin proposed a fast fix to add a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map \"businessUnit\" to \"department\" (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only change that can be hot-reloaded, thus avoiding the need to wait for Okta change control, which would take 2\u20134 weeks [art_79f625aafa16]. \n\nNo other SCIM fields besides \"department\" and \"businessUnit\" are mentioned as conflicting at Aureum in the evidence, and no additional details on the exact preprocessing rule syntax or configuration steps for the fast fix are provided beyond the high-level description [art_79f625aafa16].",
