      "answer": "The customer most likely to defect to a cheaper tactical competitor if the next promised milestone is missed is NordicChem AB. This is because they are experiencing very high alert volumes (over 32,000 alerts per day) causing on-call fatigue and procurement pressure during renewal negotiations. Procurement is explicitly considering extending a tactical proof of concept (PoC) of the competitor NoiseGuard if Northstar misses acceptance milestones, indicating a high retention risk for NordicChem AB [art_25fac9f564e7, art_ac8afb52f2d3].\n\nThe exact milestone at risk is the acceptance of the remediation plan that involves a backfill and index rebuild to restore search relevance and entity graph correctness. The milestone schedule includes:\n\n- Schema registry verification by 2026-03-22\n- Shadow index build from 2026-03-29 to 2026-04-09\n- Backfill and index weight recomputation from 2026-04-12 to 2026-04-30\n- Validation window from 2026-05-01 to 2026-05-14\n\nAcceptance criteria for this milestone are:\n\n- Precision@10 for facility lookups >= 0.8\n- Entity-link hit rate >= 90%\n- Grouping false positive rate <= 5%\n\nFailure to meet these milestones triggers a one-time 10% annual contract value credit and increases the risk that procurement will extend NoiseGuard usage, which is a cheaper tactical competitor [art_7373b64fdfdd, art_25fac9f564e7, art_a504e4c5b6f8].\n\nNo explicit identification of other customers' likelihood to defect to cheaper tactical competitors if milestones are missed, or their exact milestones, is provided in the evidence.",
