      "answer": "There is a recurring Canada approval-bypass pattern across multiple Canadian accounts after migration from legacy workflow tooling to the Orchestrator product. The affected customers are City of Verdant Bay, Maple Regional Transit Authority, MapleBay Marketplace, MapleBridge Insurance, MapleFork Franchise Systems, MaplePath Career Institute, and MapleWest Bank.\n\nThe shared failure pattern in plain English is that after migrating to the new Orchestrator system, approval workflows that should require specific approvals for Canadian regions or the country as a whole are instead being bypassed or overridden by more general global approval rules. This causes approval workflows to skip required approver nodes, approvals to be stuck or auto-denied, or approvals to route to global approvers instead of Canada-specific approvers. The root cause is a precedence bug in the rules evaluation engine where global-default policies override region-specific predicates due to differences in schema normalization, rule evaluation order, or missing priority metadata. Examples include global-default rules evaluated after or with higher precedence than province or country overrides, key name mismatches (e.g., 'country_code' vs 'country'), and delayed schema registry synchronization causing conflicts between 'canada.v2' and 'global.v3' rules.\n\nMapleBridge Insurance is not a one-off case but part of this broader recurring pattern. Its issue involved Canada-specific approval gating bypassed for certain policy types due to delayed schema synchronization and rule precedence conflicts, similar to other customers' issues. \n\nThus, the recurring pattern affects these seven customers with the same underlying cause and failure mode after migration to Orchestrator. [art_cbfb5f92862c, art_6be1b68b59cb, art_39c1434aa40a, art_f4a8c516b934, art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_981952a71434, art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_ad58f3ce1afd, art_54e35e2cb431, art_e697b3abe158, art_3db205cb21ca]",
